   "created_utc": "2014-05-02T00:07:47Z",
   "edited": false,
   "license": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
   "body_html": "This is a statically initialized array. You shouldn&#39;t be freeing it anyway."
  },
  {
   "post_type": "comment",
   "post_id": 35887764,
   "parent_id": 23418728,
   "parent_type": "question",
   "author_user_id": 2817371,
   "author_display_name": "Red Alert",
   "author_id_missing": false,
   "role": "responder",
   "is_accepted": null,
   "permalink": "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/23418728/#comment35887764_23418728",
   "score": 1,
   "created_utc": "2014-05-02T00:09:00Z",
   "edited": false,
   "license": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
   "body_html": "don&#39;t <code>free</code> something you didn&#39;t <code>malloc</code>."
  },
  {
   "post_type": "answer",
   "post_id": 23418773,
   "parent_id": 23418728,
   "author_user_id": 740696,
   "author_display_name": "Casper Beyer",
   "author_id_missing": false,
   "role": "responder",
   "is_accepted": false,
   "permalink": "https://stackoverflow.com/a/23418773",
   "score": 3,
   "created_utc": "2014-05-02T00:10:04Z",
   "last_edit_utc": "2014-05-04T19:47:09Z",
   "last_activity_utc": "2014-05-04T19:47:09Z",
   "license": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
   "body_html": "<p>If you did not allocate it (e.g <code>malloc</code>, <code>calloc</code>) then you shouldn't be deallocating it either (e.g <code>free</code>).</p>\n\n<p>Documentation will in general be very clear and explicit if you need to free a pointer returned from a function, for example <a href=\"http://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man3/strdup.3.html\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code>strdup</code></a> would be such a case.</p>\n"
  },
