   "score": 1,
   "created_utc": "2014-05-02T04:22:13Z",
   "edited": false,
   "license": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
   "body_html": "This is true in Standard C.  In POSIX and compiler extensions, sometimes you find functions that return memory you must <code>free()</code> despite the fact that you didn&#39;t malloc it. For example, <code>strdup</code> and <code>getline</code>."
  },
